{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>And HaShem said to Moses: Come up to Me on the mountain</b> — this is the command He told him the day before: \"Come up to HaShem ... and Moses alone shall approach HaShem\" (above, verses 1–2). And now, on the seventh day, He added, saying: \"and be there, and I will give you,\" for he would remain on the mountain until He would give him the tablets of stone and the Torah and the commandment. And \"which I have written\" refers back to the tablets, and \"to teach them\" to the Torah and the commandment. The proper division of the verse is: \"and I will give you the tablets of stone which I have written, and the Torah and the commandment, to teach them.\" And this is as He said in Deuteronomy (5:28): \"and I will speak to you all the commandment and the statutes and the judgments, which you shall teach them.\"\n\nRashi wrote (Rashi on Exodus 24:12): \"which I have written\" — inscribed within the stone tablets. \"To teach them\" — for all 613 commandments are contained within the Ten Commandments. And R. Abraham ibn Ezra said (Ibn Ezra on Exodus 24:12): \"the Torah\" — the first and second commandments; \"and the commandment\" — the eight that are mentioned. But none of these is correct, for the verse in Deuteronomy (ibid.) — \"and I will speak to you\" — testifies that He will speak concerning all the commandments in their entirety. And according to the opinion of our Sages (Deuteronomy Rabbah 3:12), it is possible that this is an allusion that the entire Torah was written before Him before the world was created, as I mentioned at the beginning of the book of Genesis (in the introduction)."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:18:40.538676309Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}